<!-- faktorei corpus fixture 020: PINT A-NZ Billing, the mandatory Peppol
     specification for Australia and New Zealand since 15 May 2025 (the older
     A-NZ PEPPOL BIS 3.0 extension left the network 2026-03-31). This is the
     corpus's SECOND national profile, which is what makes national profiles a
     demonstrated pattern rather than a one-off for Germany.

     Two deltas from the Peppol BIS AUD fixture (019) beyond the CustomizationID:
       · the tax scheme is GST, not VAT — the normalizer matched only 'VAT' and
         silently dropped the seller's identifier until it was taught 'GST';
       · the renderer must LABEL the tax GST, which is a jurisdiction property
         and not a language one, hence the profile-scoped label override.
     Validated against the PINT base + A-NZ jurisdiction Schematron layers,
     which do NOT include the CEN EN 16931 artefacts. -->
